   "ref": "68–73",
   "en": "Unhappy Dido burns, and wanders in her madness through the whole city — like a deer struck by an arrow, which some shepherd, [hunting|20,21] among the Cretan woods, has caught off guard and pierced from a distance, leaving the flying shaft in her without knowing it; she runs in flight through the forests and glades of Dicte, the deadly arrow still fixed in her side.",
